      # body as its own line so the detector judges the commands inside it.
      # A non-literal argument (deploy.sh uses `bash -c "$1"`) yields nothing
      # to scan and is left alone.
      # Emit a literal `-c` script as its own line so its commands are judged.
      # Recognition goes through the COMMAND WORD and the tokenizer, not a
      # regex over the whole line: `printf "%s" bash -c "..."` names an
